# Who gets asked to review what.
#
# One maintainer today, so most of this is routing rather than gatekeeping:
# GitHub requests a review from the owner of every path a pull request touches.
# The paths listed separately are the ones where a change is easy to make and
# expensive to get wrong, and they are the commitments CONTRIBUTING.md says the
# server keeps. Listing them is also a note to a future second maintainer about
# which files deserve a slower read.

*                                   @lhadhazy

# Who may read which domain: one issuer, this server's own audience, and a
# per-domain scope checked in the HTTP layer and again in every handler. A
# change here changes what a token can see.
/src/catalog_mcp/auth.py            @lhadhazy
/src/catalog_mcp/app.py             @lhadhazy

# The tools, their scope checks and their output models. Every outputSchema is
# derived from these models, and the README and the published post quote
# get_dataset's shape, so a renamed field breaks clients that validate.
/src/catalog_mcp/server.py          @lhadhazy
/src/catalog_mcp/catalog.py         @lhadhazy

# The stand-in Glue catalog, including how the IBAN columns and the source
# tables are classified. CI checks it against what the runtime writes and seeds.
/src/catalog_mcp/columns.json       @lhadhazy

# What holds this repository's restatements to the runtime: the column check,
# the lineage-identity check and the events a runtime release emitted.
/tools/                             @lhadhazy
/tests/fixtures/                    @lhadhazy

# Releases and dependencies. Pushing a `v*` tag publishes to PyPI, where a
# version number can never be reused, and the base install must stay without
# the runtime's execution stack.
/.github/workflows/                 @lhadhazy
/pyproject.toml                     @lhadhazy
/CHANGELOG.md                       @lhadhazy

# The rules every contributor and agent works to.
/AGENTS.md                          @lhadhazy
/CONTRIBUTING.md                    @lhadhazy
/SECURITY.md                        @lhadhazy
/.github/pull_request_template.md   @lhadhazy
/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/            @lhadhazy
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md                 @lhadhazy
